> It was actually {#if foo.bar != 'something' && foo.bar != 'other'} that didn't work

I'm sorry but I'm not able to reproduce it. My test looks like:
```java
Map<String, String> foo = new HashMap<>();
foo.put("bar", "1");
assertEquals("OK", engine.parse("{#if foo.bar != 'something' && foo.bar != 'other'}OK{#else}NOK{/if}").data("foo", foo).render());
```

Try:

```java
Map<String, String> foo = new HashMap<>();
foo.put("bar", "something");
assertEquals("OK", engine.parse("{#if foo.bar != 'something' && foo.bar != 'other'}OK{#else}NOK{/if}").data("foo", foo).render());

```
